contract_table=table(['Run','P50','P75','P90','P99','Mean'],[[reportlink(r['run_id'])]+[f"{r['ttft_seconds'][str(p)]:.3f} s" for p in [50,75,90,99]]+[f"{r['ttft_mean']:.3f} s"] for r in contract])
section('contract','Contract figures and current compliance limits','''<p>Tom clarified the column order as Metric, P50, P75, P90, P99, Average. The supplied TTFT targets map to 4 / 8 / 12 / 30 seconds; no average value was supplied. The stated contract tolerance is less than 1.2 times those targets. We retain the stricter research objective of short-window p50 below 4 seconds.</p>
<p>Both final runs meet all four supplied whole-run TTFT targets even before the 1.2 multiplier. This does not replace the stricter short-window research goal.</p>'''+contract_table+'''<p>The supplied speed/latency pairs are 55 tokens/s ↔ 18 ms, 30 ↔ 33 ms, and 25 ↔ 40 ms, with a speed-retention requirement above 90%. Three pairs do not fully populate the five columns. Direct OTPS percentile order reverses when converted to TPOT, and rounded reciprocals should not be treated as exact same-percentile identities. No complete contract certification is claimed yet.</p>'''+table(['ATT20 raw request metric','Observed'],[['TTFT ≤ 4 s','96.10% of successful requests'],['TPOT ≤ 18 ms','5,880 / 5,921 = 99.31%'],['TPOT ≤ 33 ms','5,911 / 5,921 = 99.83%'],['TPOT ≤ 40 ms','5,911 / 5,921 = 99.83%']])+'''<p>These are descriptive fractions using the client metric, not a reinterpretation of the contract. A request-fraction criterion and a requirement on every short-window p99 are different requirements.</p>''')
